Creates a new assumption instance for a {@link Throwable} value.

Examples:

Executed test:
<pre><code class='java'>{@literal @Test}
public void given_the_assumption_is_met_the_test_is_executed() {
  given(new Exception("Yoda time")).hasMessage("Yoda time");
  // the remaining code is executed
}</code></pre>

Skipped test:
<pre><code class='java'>{@literal @Test}
public void given_the_assumption_is_not_met_the_test_is_skipped() {
  given(new Exception("Yoda time")).hasMessage("");
  // the remaining code is NOT executed
}</code></pre>

Verifies that the actual {@code Instant} is strictly before the given one, as demonstrated in the provided example.

Example:
assertThat(parse("2007-12-03T10:15:30.00Z")).isBefore(parse("2007-12-03T10:15:31.00Z"));

// Assertion fails when the actual and expected element order differs.
assertThat(elvesRings).containsExactly(nenya, vilya, narya);

When you want to specify elements from an Iterable, use the containsExactlyElementsOf(Iterable) method instead.

// Assertion will fail when actual and expected element order differs.
assertThat(elvesRings).containsExactly(nenya, vilya, narya);

To specify the elements for checking via an Iterable collection, use the containsExactlyElementsOf method instead.

